STRING 5418
{
Support:
Those guys are the ones who provide support to their teammates. Now, that defintiion doesn't help much, since the concept of "support" is not much clear in the mind of most players. Since Ninpou is a game centered on hero killing, support is everything that aid your allies in that goal, be it stuns, holds, etc., ... Of course, most heroes can fulfill that role with substantial success, but there are heroes that stand above the others. 
Example of heroes in this category: Shikamaru, Tsunade, Chiyo, Sakura, Shino, Itachi. 
Most taijutsu heroes fit in this category, since they sacrifice damage in order to become tankier and that way providing support being a meat-shield in battle. Those heroes are called front-line support, a.k.a. tankers. They are extremely important to initiate fights and opening fog in a absence of a tracker. As a front-line support, your goal is to protect your allies at any cost, but mainly your assassin. A good communication with your assassin is a essential key to win. Recommended items: Ninja Shippu Shoes (for the speed boost, essential for starting fights), Mirror of Heaven (free you from annoying debuffs which you will certainly get since you're in front-line), Substituition Wood, Sanbi's skin (use it as long as Ninja Shippu Shoes to get both, speed boost and debuff invulnerability). Common mistakes: Not taking initiative in fights; walking too away from allies. 
Another subcategory is called back-end support. Some genjutsu heroes fit in this category. Those heroes are speciallzed in crowd-control, i.e., stuns, holds, etc., ... As a back-end support, your role is to disable the assassin of your enemy team at any cost, giving your assassin the opportunity to clear the rest. Recommended items: Poison pills (for the powerful slow and dps), Smoke bomb (slow for enemies and invisibility for allies), Kusanagi Sword (stun an enemy), Asura Essence (for the cheap hp boost). Common mistakes: Thinking you're an assassin/destroyer and rushing elemental weapon.
}

