STRING 7017
{
Tracker:
This is one of the most forgotten and ignored roles, but not less important. A tracker provides support as well, but a different kind of support that those of the support role provide. While the support role is focused in battle support, the trackers are focused in map support, be it opening fogs, be it detecting enemies, be it setting wards, be it timing and setting traps... In short, micro vs macro. Without a good tracker, you and your teammates are very susceptible to even the most obvious enemies' traps (and I see it happening a lot of time, even with S-ranks). 
Example of heroes in this category: Karin, Zetsu, Mu, Sai, Deidara, Kiba. 
As a tracker, full knowledge of map (and its vision pitfalls), flow of creeps and battle signs is essential. Your goal is: Avoid enemies' traps by opening fog and set traps by setting wards and signaling to allies. Your secondary goal is: Prevent enemies from farming by controlling creep flow and using it in your favor to set traps. Recommended items: Invisibility shoes (greater movement speed bonus than Ninja Shippu Shoes, allow you to trap enemies more easily), Bomb (a.k.a., ward. Give visibility of an area and stun who passes by. Very cheap item, high cost benefit), Mirror of Heaven (allow you to see invisible units; important to avoid being one-shotted while running through the map), lot of speed scrolls. Common mistakes: Playing too defensive; staying on base a lot; too afraid to explore the map; basically, the opposite of being a tracker.
}

